# Settle Up edge — Caddy automatic TLS (01-system-architecture.md §10).
#
# Caddy terminates TLS and reverse-proxies every request to the api service.
# The api server itself serves both `/api/*` and the built SPA from one origin.
#
# Production: set SITE_ADDRESS to the public hostname (e.g.
# `settleup.example.com`) and point its DNS record at this host. Caddy obtains
# and renews the certificate automatically on the first request — no
# certificate files to manage, no renewal cron.
#
# Local verification: the default (`SITE_ADDRESS` unset → `http://localhost`)
# serves plain HTTP on :80, so `curl -i http://localhost/` works with no
# domain. Automatic TLS is Caddy's runtime behaviour and cannot be exercised
# locally without a public domain.

{$SITE_ADDRESS:http://localhost} {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy api:3007
}
